{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["And the reason for <b>three tenth-measures for the bull</b> — for each bull among them, and likewise 'three tenth-measures for the one bull' (Numbers 28:28) means for each one among them. And <b>for the one lamb</b> (Numbers 28:21) is inferred from His saying <b>a tenth-measure, a tenth-measure</b>, and further He specifies <b>for the seven lambs</b>. And likewise this <b>for the bull</b>, the one — for the two bulls. But at times Scripture abbreviates in a matter that is understood, for it is known that there would not be three tenth-measures for the one bull and nothing at all for the second. And He specifies concerning the lambs, which are numerous, all the more so concerning the bulls. And in Sukkot, where the bulls are numerous, He specifies concerning them: 'for thirteen bulls' (Numbers 29:14)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:09:25.917882322Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}